  "oneLinerQuestion": "Find the minimum water height/time needed to travel from top-left to bottom-right of a grid.",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/swim-in-rising-water/",
  "explanation": "Dijkstra's Algorithm using Min-Heap: track path maximum grid elevation. Always expand the adjacent unvisited neighbor requiring minimal water height.",
  "pseudoCode": "FUNCTION swimInWater(grid):\n    N = LENGTH(grid), minHeap = MinHeap([[grid[0][0], 0, 0]]), visit = SET([(0,0)])\n    WHILE minHeap DO:\n        [t, r, c] = POP(minHeap)\n        IF r == N - 1 AND c == N - 1 THEN RETURN t\n        FOR dr, dc IN [[1,0], [-1,0], [0,1], [0,-1]] DO:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            IF nr >= 0 AND nc >= 0 AND nr < N AND nc < N AND (nr,nc) NOT IN visit THEN:\n                ADD (nr,nc) TO visit\n                PUSH [MAX(t, grid[nr][nc]), nr, nc] TO minHeap\n            END IF\n        END FOR\n    END WHILE\nEND FUNCTION",
